{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/955007-2e-anchors-why-not-flux","id":955007,"title":"[2E] Anchors - Why not Flux?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T10:20:41-07:00","id":955007,"title":"[2E] Anchors - Why not Flux?","content":"One thing that is very weird to me in game design is names for characters Anchors in 2E. I understand that Elpis is positive, Virtue equivalent - it has sense that it's force that calls Created to do greater things.<br /> <br /> Weird to me is choosing Torment as Vice equivalent - Torments are different based on mostly Linage, much lesser on current character Refinement. There is very much 'Vice' in it - it's much more 'Humor imbalance' of character.<br /> <br /> <b>Not better would pairing Elpis with Flux as Anchors?</b> This would clearly show that Prometheans have both sides of Pyros in them and that Flux is impuls in characters. Also, it would leave Torment as very individual reaction, mix of many circumstances, not the characters define trait.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:18:41-07:00","id":955222,"title":"","content":"Short answer: it gives players an intuitive link between their &quot;vice&quot; and going into rage-mode.<br /> <br /> On phone, longer answer later","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:33:11-07:00","id":955314,"title":"","content":"Ok so. Long answer.<br /> <br /> There's a concept in game design which basically states that no element of your game should do a single thing. The more the better, basically. Virtue and Vice, from the start, serve two purposes: they create drama (important in an RPG) and they allow for willpower recovery. They also tie into the soul loss system and are hooks for many conditions, plus they serve as weaknesses when in social maneuvering.<br /> <br /> Shifting to Promethean, you get a similar thing in your Virtue (Elpis) but most importantly, by deciding to pick Torment rather than Flux, you hook your system to your narrative in a lot of new ways. In 1st edition, Torment was Frenzy. You lost control and did weird shit based on your lineage. It was the crazy button, and it was hard for an ST to drive the point that Torment was the <i>constant</i> desire to be a monster, the nibbling envy of losing control over oneself. By hooking one of the Torment triggers to your &quot;vice&quot;, and by naming your vice &quot;torment&quot;, you drive home, subconsciously, that Torment is a constant thing in the Promethean's life, not just a random &quot;Oh shit!&quot; moment that happens every now and then (looking at you, Exalted 2nd edition)<br /> <br /> You can see such a design philosophy in <i>many</i> places in Promethean. Completing Roles gives new powers. Refinements giving a condition. Vitriol being a physical thing in the game. And many others.<br /> <br /> If Matt would've gone with simply Elpis &amp; Flux, well.... it wouldn't have been a whole lot different from virtue and vice (at best) or it would've felt a little dissonant (at worst).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T03:51:36-07:00","id":955507,"title":"","content":"One thing that comes to mind around Anchors - What is difference between Azoth and Elpis? As both sound from corebook like 'positive' parts of Pyros and both are putted against Flux.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T07:40:03-07:00","id":955574,"title":"","content":"Azoth is the &quot;evolution&quot; side of Pyros.<br /> Flux is the &quot;mutation&quot; side of Pyros.<br /> Elpis is hope, the force that drives a Promethean on its pilgrimage<br /> Torment is the feeling that you don't belong in this world<br /> <br /> As such, Elpis and Torment are way better as Virtue/vice<br /> <br /> (All of the above are tl;dr from the 2nd edition Glossary)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-29T20:03:31-07:00","id":960187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/955007-2e-anchors-why-not-flux?p=955507#post955507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is difference between Azoth and Elpis?</div> </div> </div> </div>To fully understand my reply, do please read both posts what <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus\">Magnum Opus</a></b> wrote, above... And then realise that what I write below may not be anything like the 'truth' at all.<br /> <br /> Azoth and Flux, put simply, ARE the Divine Fire, or they're aspects of the Divine Fire's possible outcomes. Pyros is, in this analogy at least, the HEAT of the Divine Fire, the part of it that does WORK in terms of what energy does from a physics perspective, and as such Pyros is completely neutral in whether it serves the ends of Azoth or Flux. Then the Principle is the part of the Divine Fire that might think/feel/plan or whatever a 'person' might understand as the purpose of a personality, but the Divine Fire is so alien to people as to make such statements pointless. Hell, even the qashmallim, who act as surrogates for the Principle when it must interact with the world are nigh impossible for a living \u2013 or close to living, as the case may be \u2013 to fathom. All of this plays into what one of the Created needs to grasp in order to follow or reject the Pilgrimage, and those mechanisms are the Anchors in the game. Thus, Elpis and Torment (a name I'm not crazy about only because it describes at least two other things in the game) are dependent upon but external from the Divine Fire. <br /> <br /> Elpis is the approach to the Divine Fire that urges one of the Created toward the goal of the New Dawn, all that junk that says, 'It will be worth it in the end, if you make it that far.' Elpis IS hope, of course, but it is also the reminders that the Azoth burning inside is NOT a soul, not yet. It's not all sweet and warm because it remains a reminder of what the Promethean does not have, what she so dearly wants to have.<br /> <br /> Torment reflects an approach to the New Dawn that it's just NOT worth it, no matter what Azothic Memory says, no matter who knows a bloke who met a woman who finished her Magnum Opus. It's not just an ABSENCE of hope, but it does fly in the face of what Elpis offers. On the other hand, Torment does give a clue at what it means to be human when confronted with something that is completely un-natural, something that the mind and soul refuse to accept. Torment can be the nasty side of the New Dawn, those bits of the human experience that humans don't like to admit are vital to us being, well... human.<br /> <br /> ...The above is MY interpretation of it, sure, but it also offers what <b>Magnum Opus</b> said about these traits doing 'more than one thing' in the game. Just as Virtue and Vice aren't synonymous with 'good' and 'bad', respectively, so too aren't Elpis and Torment. Each offers one of the Created a perfectly useful way to interact with her place \u2013 or lack thereof \u2013 in the world. Dunno if it's really, really helpful, but the players in my troupe quite dug my version. Maybe it'll help you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}